workedExamples.solution_text:
For $P$, start at the origin, move $2$ units left, then $1$ unit up. Mark and label the point.

For $Q$, move $1.5$ units right, then $1.5$ units down. Both coordinates fall halfway between integer gridlines.
[tikz]
\begin{tikzpicture}[x=8mm,y=8mm,font=\fontsize{10}{12}\selectfont]
\definecolor{gridcolour}{HTML}{CCCCCC}
\definecolor{answerblue}{HTML}{268CFF}
\draw[step=4mm,gridcolour] (-3,-3) grid (3,3);
\draw[<->,black] (-3.3,0)--(3.3,0);
\draw[<->,black] (0,-3.3)--(0,3.3);
\path (3.3,0) node[right,text=black] {$x$} (0,3.3) node[above,text=black] {$y$};
\foreach \v in {-3,-2,-1,1,2,3} {\path (\v,0) node[below,text=black,font=\fontsize{8.5}{10}\selectfont] {$\v$};\path (0,\v) node[left,text=black,font=\fontsize{8.5}{10}\selectfont] {$\v$};}
\draw[->,dashed,answerblue] (0,0)--(-2,0);
\draw[->,dashed,answerblue] (-2,0)--(-2,1);
\draw[->,dashed,answerblue] (0,0)--(1.5,0);
\draw[->,dashed,answerblue] (1.5,0)--(1.5,-1.5);
\fill[answerblue] (-2,1) circle (1.5pt) (1.5,-1.5) circle (1.5pt);
\path (-2,1) node[above left,text=answerblue] {$P$} (1.5,-1.5) node[below right,text=answerblue] {$Q$};
\end{tikzpicture}
[/tikz]

(a) $A$ and $B$ both have $x=-1.5$, so they line up vertically. $B$ and $C$ both have $y=-1$, so they line up horizontally.

(b) $D$ keeps $A$'s $x$-coordinate. On the $x$-axis, $y=0$, so $D=(-1.5,0)$.

(c) $E$ keeps $C$'s $y$-coordinate. On the $y$-axis, $x=0$, so $E=(0,-1)$.
[tikz]
\begin{tikzpicture}[x=8mm,y=8mm,font=\fontsize{10}{12}\selectfont]
\definecolor{gridcolour}{HTML}{CCCCCC}
\definecolor{answerblue}{HTML}{268CFF}
\draw[step=4mm,gridcolour] (-3,-2) grid (3,3);
\draw[<->,black] (-3.3,0)--(3.3,0);
\draw[<->,black] (0,-2.3)--(0,3.3);
\path (3.3,0) node[right,text=black] {$x$} (0,3.3) node[above,text=black] {$y$};
\foreach \v in {-3,-2,-1,1,2,3} {\path (\v,0) node[below,text=black,font=\fontsize{8.5}{10}\selectfont] {$\v$};}
\foreach \v in {-2,-1,1,2,3} {\path (0,\v) node[left,text=black,font=\fontsize{8.5}{10}\selectfont] {$\v$};}
\draw[dashed,answerblue] (-1.5,2)--(-1.5,-1)--(2,-1);
\fill[black] (-1.5,2) circle (1.5pt) (-1.5,-1) circle (1.5pt) (2,-1) circle (1.5pt);
\path (-1.5,2) node[above left,text=black] {$A$} (-1.5,-1) node[below left,text=black] {$B$} (2,-1) node[below right,text=black] {$C$};
\fill[answerblue] (-1.5,0) circle (1.5pt) (0,-1) circle (1.5pt);
\path (-1.5,0) node[above left,text=answerblue] {$D$} (0,-1) node[above right,text=answerblue] {$E$};
\end{tikzpicture}
[/tikz]

