\path (-1,2.5) node[above left] {$A(-1,2.5)$} (3,2.5) node[above right] {$B(3,2.5)$} (3,-2) node[below right] {$C(3,-2)$};
\end{tikzpicture}
[/tikz]

workedExamples.solution_text:
$D$ is directly below $A$, so $x=-1$. It is directly left of $C$, so $y=-2$.

$D=(-1,-2)$.
[tikz]
\begin{tikzpicture}[x=9mm,y=9mm,font=\fontsize{10}{12}\selectfont]
\definecolor{answerblue}{HTML}{268CFF}
\draw[black] (-1,2.5)--(3,2.5)--(3,-2);
\draw[answerblue] (3,-2)--(-1,-2)--(-1,2.5);
\fill[black] (-1,2.5) circle (1.5pt) (3,2.5) circle (1.5pt) (3,-2) circle (1.5pt);
\fill[answerblue] (-1,-2) circle (1.5pt);
\path (-1,2.5) node[above left,text=black] {$A(-1,2.5)$} (3,2.5) node[above right,text=black] {$B(3,2.5)$} (3,-2) node[below right,text=black] {$C(3,-2)$} (-1,-2) node[below left,text=answerblue] {$D(-1,-2)$};
\end{tikzpicture}
[/tikz]

